description:
Design a 3-bit binary to Gray code converter that operates on the rising edge of a clock signal (CLK). The module takes a 3-bit binary input (BIN) and generates a corresponding 3-bit Gray code output (GRAY). The most significant bit of the Gray code is directly copied from the binary input, while the other bits are computed using bitwise XOR operations between the relevant bits of the binary input. This functionality is useful for applications where Gray code is preferred to minimize errors during transitions.
module top_module(
    input [2:0] BIN,
    input CLK,
    output reg [2:0] GRAY
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [2:0] BIN,
    input CLK,
    output reg [2:0] GRAY
);always @(posedge CLK) begin
    GRAY[2] <= BIN[2];
    GRAY[1] <= BIN[2] ^ BIN[1];
    GRAY[0] <= BIN[1] ^ BIN[0];
end

endmodule

