description:
Design a clock generation module that produces a divided clock signal based on an external clock input and an active control signal. When the active signal is low, the output `system_clk` is set to low. When active, the module increments a 32-bit counter on each rising edge of the input clock. Every time the counter reaches 100, the output clock `system_clk` toggles its state. This effectively divides the input clock frequency by 200 (considering both rising edges of the output clock), allowing for slower clock operations in a system where lower frequencies are required.
module top_module(
    input [0:0] clk,
    input active,
    output reg system_clk
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input [0:0] clk,
    input active,
    output reg system_clk
    );reg [31:0] clk_counter = 32'd0;
		always @(posedge clk) begin
				if (~active)
				begin
					system_clk = 1'd0;
				end
				else 
				begin
					if(clk_counter == 32'd100) 
					begin
						system_clk = ~system_clk;
						clk_counter = 16'd0;
					end
					else begin
						clk_counter = clk_counter+1'd1;
					end
				end
		end
endmodule

