Design a digital clock circuit that counts minutes and hours based on a provided clock signal. The module increments the minute output every minute, and when minutes reach 60, it resets to 0 and increments the hour output. The hour output resets to 0 after reaching 16 (representing a 24-hour cycle). A 24-bit counter tracks time elapsed from the clock signal to ensure accurate minute updates.
