description:
Design a state control interface unit that manages the initiation and termination of a process based on asynchronous input signals. It features a two-way control mechanism: when the `reset` or `done` signals are activated, it resets the `start` output to LOW. Conversely, when receiving a `start_asyn` signal, the `start` output is set based on that input. Additionally, the `done_moore` output is controlled by the clock in relation to the `reset` and `done` signals, resetting when `start_asyn` is received or when the module is reset, effectively indicating process completion only when `done` is HIGH. This module is designed to synchronize and control signal transitions in sequential processing.
module top_module(
	input clock, reset, start_asyn, done,
	output reg start, done_moore
);

code:
module top_module(
	input clock, reset, start_asyn, done,
	output reg start, done_moore
);always@(posedge clock or posedge reset or posedge done)
begin
	if (reset == 1 || done == 1)
		start <= 1'b0;
	else
		start <= start_asyn;
end


always@(posedge clock or posedge reset or posedge start_asyn)
begin
	if(reset == 1 || start_asyn == 1)
		done_moore = 1'b0;
	else
	if (done == 1)
		done_moore <= done;
end
endmodule

