description:
Design a bus hold block that captures and holds a multi-bit bus value when the enable signal is active. When enable is high, the value present on the bus is latched into a register; when enable is low, the output presents a high-impedance state. This circuit effectively retains the last valid bus value until the next activation of the enable signal, allowing for controlled data flow in a digital system.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] bus,
  input enable,
  output [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] bus,
  input enable,
  output [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 8; // number of bits in the bus

reg [n-1:0] latch;

always @(posedge enable) begin
  if (enable) begin
    latch <= bus;
  end
end

assign out = enable ? 'bz : latch;

endmodule

